y "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-276787/field-4/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer-field/choices ["q-276787/field-4/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-276787" :question/id #uuid "b15e89bf-dbe4-54e6-8d2f-e2da97637055" :question/math-academy-id "q-276787" :question/problem "Given the polynomial $P(x)=-x(x+3)(x-2)(x-4),$ find the solution of $P(x)<0.$\n\n$x\\in (\\,-\\infty ,$\n{{field-1}}$)⋃($\n{{field-2}}$,\\,2)⋃($\n{{field-3}}$,$\n{{field-4}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality $P(x)<0,$ we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=P(x)$ lies below the $x$-axis.\n\nThe roots of the polynomial $P(x)=-x(x+3)(x-2)(x-4)$ are $x=-3,$ $x=0,$ $x=2$ and $x=4,$ which are all simple roots.\n\nAlso, $P(x)$ is a quartic polynomial with a negative leading coefficient. So, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/assets/889f60e9a8dac71f99dd7e676b77c3e0a1eb7b944305e21b9d4d1b6897dbbb15.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $P(x)<0,$ we look for the part of the curve that is below the $x$-axis.\n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\in (-\\infty ,-3)⋃(0,2)⋃(4,\\infty ).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-276787/field-1" "q-276787/field-2" "q-276787/field-3" "q-276787/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64b71f10-5b2b-5cae-a5dc-b9c160484d82"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-276787"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-40270"] :question/problem "Given the polynomial $P(x)=(x+2)(x-1)(x-2),$ find the solution of $P(x)>0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality $P(x)>0,$ we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=P(x)$ lies above the $x$-axis.\n\nThe roots of the polynomial $P(x)=(x+2)(x-1)(x-2)$ are $x=1$ and $x=\\pm 2,$ which are all simple roots.\n\nAlso, $P(x)$ is a cubic polynomial with a positive leading coefficient. So, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/assets/65a899ed4375be4681c0e4598cc4769335cabb52257a886148438f4b4f16e671.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $P(x)>0,$ we look for the part of the curve that is above the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\in (-2,1)\\cup (2,\\infty ).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-40188/selection/d8f949ceaeed8d2f60dcd33a7737f30f9d2dad3eb1e5dfa1b800ab9646136e8f" :answer/id #uuid "36599804-6e0f-5b77-8112-b74cfae3d331" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40188/selection/619df3d5fd2838bd6bde1528623761cbdf17c18a2799472e2526cb70e2ec06d3" :answer/id #uuid "4b04c719-cf75-5c30-83db-c657d65979cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-3,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40188/selection/e358f7f1f4263ad4bff65aad3f9f9c42eb88cc994e556e928b4e8d67857db542" :answer/id #uuid "a5125261-e7a9-5a8e-98d0-e134c04b1c01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (1,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40188/selection/dc25ac3aaa0c3d5df6a9c8d388bfec2ab9cea4e44455238784d492867db76674" :answer/id #uuid "082836b6-734f-5344-8742-2512bc493410" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (1,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40188/selection/855a174ab24d8ffcc672b5948406119dc0ce9d4de8fda79a37dc7cc59e9a01c8" :answer/id #uuid "89f1248f-676d-590a-8667-c07ed831bad0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (-3,0)\\cup (1,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40188/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d0c6a6ef-4136-5c79-8544-