4x+3x-12) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}(x(x-4)+3(x-4)) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}(x+3)(x-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe roots of the polynomial $P(x)=12{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}-{x}^{4}$ are $x=-3,$ $x=0$ and $x=4,$ where\n\n- $x=0$ has multiplicity $2,$ and\n\n- $x=-3$ and $x=4$ are simple roots.\n\nSo, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/assets/5ebfbd4e18de00fad05c4192be2147a9b9765e00fae5b74ac608e85466c21e73.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $P(x)>0,$ we look for the part of the curve that is above the $x$-axis.\n\nBased on the graph, the solution is \n\n$$\nx\\in (-3,0)\\cup (0,4).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-87672/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "48de9cc7-5f86-51e4-a827-796f77381af2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-87672"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-116437/selection/1cb833294f700b747a0afb39b62f4529e6eff1cddea736cbb0d78f36c6481df1" :answer/id #uuid "15cfb5b0-1833-5d4f-a6a6-ef2f79b7e99c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (2,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116437/selection/5a2fff3f4361c4773b8bfd62b219d9ad0aa450150b947642ad4fc012a087b8f9" :answer/id #uuid "b9a3a969-ac7a-564f-bc17-17a54d317c15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-2,2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116437/selection/e8411a78bc421eca6b0e364a6591218e671ce07b413b8c45807af63ca4af00f4" :answer/id #uuid "6320b40c-f6bb-5cbc-8620-982123e47091" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-4,0)\\cup (4,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116437/selection/dad289050313bb725fe1bfe30ccb9e3e0eebfa5243173f1f5356c8e1d93ae959" :answer/id #uuid "877939eb-60b5-5803-a2f9-6b4598ea50e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-2,0)\\cup (0,2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116437/selection/1db9831